<h1>BEATZ: Product & Technical Implementation Plan</h1>
<div class="subtitle">1-Week Sprint MVP: AI-Powered Spotify Web Player & Queue Manager | Architecture & Division of Labor</div>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>The Beatz Advantage:</strong><br>
  <strong>1. Free On-Demand Listening:</strong> Unlike Spotify Free which locks mobile users into forced shuffle, Beatz unlocks 100% on-demand song choice for free (funded by a higher ad density: 3–5 ads/hr, 45s–2.5m).<br>
  <strong>2. Interactive AI Music Chatbot ("Beatz AI"):</strong> Spotify has no conversational chatbot. Beatz integrates an AI co-pilot that curates queues, shifts vibes, and explains song lore via natural language.
</div>

<h2>1. Executive Summary & Partnership Roles</h2>
<p>To eliminate inter-team blocking and maximize velocity, this sprint adopts a <strong>Contract-First Architecture</strong>. Work is strictly divided across domain boundaries:</p>

<div class="role-box">
  <div class="role-title"><span class="badge badge-be">Backend & API Architecture Lead</span> (Your Scope)</div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Authentication & Security:</strong> Spotify OAuth 2.0 PKCE flow, access & refresh token rotation.</li>
    <li><strong>Audio Streaming Engine:</strong> Spotify Web Playback SDK integration, device ID registration, and playback transfer.</li>
    <li><strong>REST API Wrappers:</strong> Resilient fetch endpoints for active queue (<code>GET /queue</code>, <code>POST /queue</code>) and catalog search.</li>
    <li><strong>AI Chatbot Engine (<code>/api/chat</code>):</strong> LLM integration with function calling to auto-queue songs, play tracks, and fetch song lore.</li>
    <li><strong>Ad Scheduler Engine:</strong> State machine running 3–5 ad breaks per hour (45s–2.5m) that pauses the SDK stream and locks controls.</li>
    <li><strong>Zustand State & Custom Hooks:</strong> <code>useSpotifyPlayer</code>, <code>useSpotifyQueue</code>, and <code>useBeatzChat</code> so frontend never touches raw fetch requests.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="role-box">
  <div class="role-title"><span class="badge badge-fe">Frontend & UI/UX Design Lead</span> (Erick's Scope)</div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Design System:</strong> Modern dark Spotify theme (Tailwind tokens, typography, active status indicators).</li>
    <li><strong>Sticky Player Bar:</strong> Responsive bottom dock containing album art, track title, scrubber slider, transport buttons, and volume control.</li>
    <li><strong>Interactive Queue Drawer:</strong> Slide-over panel displaying current song and upcoming queue list with reorder/remove UI.</li>
    <li><strong>Beatz AI Chatbot Widget:</strong> Slide-over chat interface with message bubbles, quick prompt chips (<em>"⚡ Boost Energy"</em>, <em>"🧠 Focus Lo-Fi"</em>), and playable track recommendation cards.</li>
    <li><strong>Ad Interstitial Overlay:</strong> Visual countdown overlay displayed during ad breaks (<em>"Ad break in progress: 1:30 remaining"</em>).</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<h2>2. Day-by-Day Parallel Execution Matrix</h2>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 10%;">Day</th>
      <th style="width: 45%;">Backend & API Track (You)</th>
      <th style="width: 45%;">Frontend & UI Track (Erick)</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Day 1</strong></td>
      <td>Register Spotify App; setup OAuth 2.0 PKCE flow; implement token storage and refresh logic.</td>
      <td>Scaffold Next.js + Tailwind project; define color tokens; create base application layout shell.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Day 2</strong></td>
      <td>Build API client (<code>lib/spotify.ts</code>) with mock fallback responses; implement track search and queue wrappers.</td>
      <td>Build static <code>PlayerBar</code> UI using mock track data; design transport controls, scrubber slider, and album art layout.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Day 3</strong></td>
      <td>Inject Web Playback SDK script; implement <code>window.Spotify.Player</code> lifecycle listeners (ready, error, state_changed).</td>
      <td>Build static <code>QueueDrawer</code> slide-over component with mock song queue; implement open/close transitions.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Day 4</strong></td>
      <td>Build Zustand global store (<code>usePlayerStore</code>); implement Ad Scheduler engine (3–5 ads/hr, 45s–2.5m).</td>
      <td>Hook up <code>PlayerBar</code> to the Zustand store hooks; design Ad countdown banner overlay.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Day 5</strong></td>
      <td>Build <code>/api/chat</code> route with LLM tool calling (<code>search_and_queue</code>, <code>play_track</code>, <code>get_context</code>).</td>
      <td>Build <code>BeatzChat</code> slide-over drawer with prompt chips, chat history, and playable recommendation cards.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Day 6</strong></td>
      <td>Connect Chatbot tools to live player state; handle edge cases: Non-Premium 403 alert, token auto-refresh.</td>
      <td>Responsive design polish (mobile bottom sheet vs desktop dock), hover states, volume transitions, empty states.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Day 7</strong></td>
      <td>Integration verification (Auth &rarr; Stream &rarr; Queue &rarr; Chat &rarr; Ads); Vercel deployment.</td>
      <td>Final design polish, typography consistency, presentation slides prep, live demo smoke testing.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>3. Updated Email Cover Note to Erick</h2>
<div style="background-color: #f1f5f9; padding: 14px; border: 1px dashed #94a3b8; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 10.5pt;">
  Hi Erick,<br><br>
  I’ve updated our master project plan for <strong>Beatz</strong> with our two major competitive differentiators:<br>
  1. <strong>Free On-Demand Listening:</strong> We allow users to pick and play any song on demand (unlike Spotify Free which forces shuffle on mobile), supported by a higher ad density (3–5 ads/hr, 45s–2.5m).<br>
  2. <strong>AI Music Chatbot ("Beatz AI"):</strong> Spotify has no chatbot. We're embedding an interactive AI co-pilot that can curate queues and chat about music via natural language.<br><br>
  I’ve mapped out how this divides across our backend (LLM tool calling, ad scheduler) and frontend (chat drawer, ad banner) roles in the attached doc. Let's look it over together!
</div>

